## Hartwig and Siegel Severity Assessment Scale

* Severity Rating: Level 4 (b) - Moderate
* Classification Criteria: Any ADR that requires drug withdrawal, initiation of specific secondary treatment (IVIG / alternative anticoagulant), and causes an increase in hospital length of stay by at least 1 day.
* Clinical Justification: The reaction required immediate heparin withdrawal, introduction of alternative non-heparin anticoagulation, IVIG administration, and extended monitoring in the hospital to ensure platelet recovery and prevent arterial/venous thrombosis.
